{"raw": {"https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Term-Faculty---Stage-Management_JR009322": {"title": "Term Faculty | Stage Management", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nJoin our \u00a0 community \u00a0 and experience \u00a0 Emerson College! Emerson College\u2019s Department of Performing Arts invites applications for a fulltime faculty term position in Stage Management for our BFA in Design and Stage Management. The appointment begins August 19, 2027 with a mandatory 2-day orientation August 19 & 20, 2027.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Emerson\u2019s Department of Performing Arts is home to one of the nation\u2019s leading undergraduate programs with robust offerings in acting and performance, design, stage management, and theatre education. Our programs engage 80 full- and part-time faculty members and staff with 525 students studying in five distinct BFA\u2019s and one graduate program. The Performing Arts Department is supported by its own producing organization, Emerson Stage, in which the students work alongside our staff and industry professionals throughout 5 different venues to bring 8 to 10 fully produced, high quality productions to life annually.\u00a0 This is an in-person teaching position based at Emerson's Boston campus. Term faculty appointments are renewable and begin with a one-year contract, with the opportunity to advance to longer multi-year terms based on periodic performance review.\u00a0 PRIMARY JOB DUTIES: This position carries a 3/3 course load, teaching 6 classes over the academic year. Teaching responsibilities for this position could include, but are not limited to, the following courses in our Design and Stage Management BFA curriculum:\u00a0 Stage Management Course Sequence 1 - 4\u00a0 Mentoring colloquium\u00a0 Arts Management Courses (If applicable)\u00a0 Production Management (If applicable) Service responsibilities will include: Provide leadership to the Stage Management concentration Academic Advising Recruitment, interviews of prospective\u00a0 students, and retention initiatives Support and mentorship for career placement\u00a0 Other service as assigned by the area and department QUALIFICATIONS:\u00a0 The candidate will have a degree (Bachelors or MFA) in Stage Management or related areas with at least 5 years professional experience in theatre and one or more of the following forms: opera, dance, immersive, tours, events, etc. Experience in Arts Management and Production Management is a plus but not required. Applicants must have significant experience in teaching Stage Management at the college level. Membership in Actor\u2019s Equity and USITT is required. Affiliations to IATSE, AGMA, or other professional organizations are preferred.\u00a0 SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS:\u00a0 Please submit the following documents: Cover Letter\u00a0 Curriculum Vitae Statement of teaching philosophy that addresses both the candidate\u2019s approach to mentorship and how the candidate creates learning environments in which everyone has the opportunity to excel. Support materials/links to professional work that demonstrates professional processes (paperwork and prompt books are examples).\u00a0 Contact information for three references who can speak to the candidate\u2019s professional work and/or teaching.\u00a0 Preference will be given to applications received by November 23, but the position will remain open until filled. Please note that finalists will be invited to campus for in-person teaching demonstrations and interviews during the Spring semester. Please note, in the job application where there is the \"CV/Cover Letter/Additional Documents\" drop box, you must include all of the required materials listed above. You can upload each document separately or as a combined PDF. Your application will not be complete without these documents. If you are having issues uploading, please email facultycareers@emerson.edu. Base salary for this appointment, as set by the CBA, will be $81,723 annually. Additional salary, supplements, and/or stipends may be available and applicable. Emerson College is the nation\u2019s only four-year institution dedicated exclusively to undergraduate majors and master\u2019s in communication, arts, and media. It is located in the dynamic, multicultural city of Boston, close to major arts institutions, performing arts venues, research centers, and industry partners. Emerson also has campuses in Los Angeles and the Netherlands. At Emerson College, we seek individuals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to our curricular, co-curricular, and extra-curricular offerings. Emerson College believes the best way to achieve excellence is to foster a campus climate where everyone can thrive. As a community of artists, practitioners, scholars, and storytellers, we continually strive to cultivate a collaborative community that draws upon the widest possible pool of talented individuals from varied beliefs, backgrounds, and perspectives. Emerson College\u2019s core values are creativity, innovation, inclusion, curiosity, equity, expression, and collaboration."}, "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Open-Rank--Term-or-Tenure-Track-Tenured-----On-Camera-Acting-and-Scene-Study_JR009321-1": {"title": "Open Rank (Term or Tenure-Track/Tenured) |  On-Camera Acting and Scene Study", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nJoin our \u00a0 community \u00a0 and experience \u00a0 Emerson College! The Department of Performing Arts invites applications for a full time position in On-Camera Acting and Scene Study for our BFA Acting Program. This is an open rank position, commensurate with experience, of Tenured (Associate or Full Professor), Tenure Track (Assistant Professor), Artist-In-Residence or Distinguished-Artist-in-Residence (both full-time, non-tenure-track). The Department seeks a creative, accomplished, and deeply engaged actor and educator. The appointment begins August 19, 2027 with a mandatory 2-day orientation August 19 & 20, 2027.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The Department of Performing Arts is home to one of the nation's leading undergraduate programs in theatrical performance and production, with 97 full and part time faculty members and staff and 550 students across all disciplines. The department offers BFAs in Acting; Design and Stage Management; Musical Theatre; Playwriting, Directing, and Dramaturgy; and Theatre Education and Performance, as well as an MA in Theatre Education and Applied Theatre. Emerson Stage presents up to nine fully staged productions annually in five theaters, with additional production opportunities available to our students through ArtsEmerson, our nationally and internationally-recognized professional presenting company.\u00a0 This is an in-person teaching position based at Emerson's Boston campus. ESSENTIAL JOB DUTIES Primary responsibilities for this position include teaching classes in On Camera Acting, Scene Study, and The Business of Acting/Professional Prep to our BFA Acting students. Other potential course assignments might include advanced acting classes based on the candidate's areas of expertise. Depending on rank, this position either carries a 3/3 course load teaching 6 classes over the academic year (for an Artist-in-Residence Rank), or a 3/2 course load teaching 5 classes over the academic year (for the rank of Tenured or Tenure Track). Additional responsibilities include mentoring students, assisting in the admissions audition process, advising on Emerson Stage, serving on department and college committees, and participating in the college\u2019s system of shared governance. QUALIFICATIONS\u00a0 The candidate must have notable film and television credits on IMDB, and be a member of SAG/AFTRA. The ideal candidate will hold an MFA in Acting or a related field. Additionally, our ideal candidate will be able to teach coursework focused on cultivating actor-creators:\u00a0 performers who make their own work, especially for the camera.\u00a0 Candidates must be experienced teachers of acting, at the college level or in a professional studio setting.\u00a0 INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS\u00a0 Please submit the following: Cover letter summarizing and further illuminating pertinent aspects of your professional background and perspectives that are relevant to this position A separate document listing all special topics classes you can teach besides On Camera Acting and Scene Study Curriculum Vita A statement of teaching philosophy that includes specifics on\u00a0 your curricular approach to Acting for the Camera\u00a0 how you might teach the development of the actor-creator within your classroom Demonstration of teaching excellence via teaching evaluation or student testimonials\u00a0 Names and contact information for three references\u00a0 Optional: support materials/links to professional work Priority will be given to applications received by November 20th , but review of applications will continue until an appointment is made. Please note: In the job application where there is the \"CV/Cover Letter/Additional Documents\" drop box, you must include all of the required materials listed above. You can upload each document separately or as a combined PDF. Your application will not be complete without these documents. If you are having issues uploading, please email facultycareers@emerson.edu Base salary for this appointment, as set by the CBA, will be $81,723 - $109,042 annually, commensurate with experience and rank of position. Additional salary, supplements, and/or stipends may be available and applicable. Emerson College is the nation\u2019s only four-year institution dedicated exclusively to undergraduate majors and master\u2019s in communication, arts, and media. It is located in the dynamic, multicultural city of Boston, close to major arts institutions, performing arts venues, research centers, and industry partners. Emerson also has campuses in Los Angeles and the Netherlands. At Emerson College, we seek individuals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to our curricular, co-curricular, and extra-curricular offerings. Emerson College believes the best way to achieve excellence is to foster a campus climate where everyone can thrive. As a community of artists, practitioners, scholars, and storytellers, we continually strive to cultivate a collaborative community that draws upon the widest possible pool of talented individuals from varied beliefs, backgrounds, and perspectives. Emerson College\u2019s core values are creativity, innovation, inclusion, curiosity, equity, expression, and collaboration."}, "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Term-Faculty---Lighting-Design_JR009298": {"title": "Term Faculty | Lighting Design", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJoin our \u00a0 community \u00a0 and experience \u00a0 Emerson College! The BFA program in Design and Stage Management and the Department of Performing Arts invite applications for a full-time Term Faculty in Lighting Design. We seek a creative, accomplished, and deeply engaged lighting designer and educator with experience in the field of lighting for live performances (theatre, opera, dance, or concert) and adjacent fields (film, TV, corporate, or museums) to join our community. \u00a0The appointment begins August 19, 2027, with a mandatory 2-day orientation on August 19 & 20, 2027.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 The Department of Performing Arts is home to one of the nation's leading undergraduate programs in theatrical performance and production, with 97 full- and part-time faculty members and staff and 550 students across all disciplines. The department offers BFAs in Acting; Design and Stage Management; Musical Theatre; Playwriting, Directing, and Dramaturgy; and Theatre Education and Performance \u2013 and an MA in Theatre Education and Applied Theatre. Emerson Stage presents up to nine fully staged productions annually in five theaters, with additional production opportunities available to our students through ArtsEmerson, our nationally and internationally recognized professional presenting company.\u00a0 This is an in-person teaching position based at Emerson's Boston campus. Term faculty appointments are renewable and begin with a one-year contract, with the opportunity to advance to longer multi-year terms based on periodic performance review.\u00a0 Primary Duties and Responsibilities This position carries a 3/3 course load, teaching 6 classes over the academic year. Primary teaching responsibilities for this position include, but are not limited to, the following courses in our Design and Stage Management BFA curriculum:\u00a0 Lighting Design I Lighting Design II Foundations of Stage Design Drafting I and II (Hand Drafting and Vectorworks) Electrics Programming Additional service responsibilities will include: Academic advising Recruitment, interviews of perspective students, and retention Initiatives Support and mentorship for senior showcase curriculum\u00a0 Provide leadership to the lighting concentration Other service as assigned by the area and department Qualifications\u00a0 The ideal candidate will hold an MFA in Lighting Design or an undergraduate Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Design accompanied by at least 3-5 years professional experience. Candidates should demonstrate their professional practice through LORT, regional, or commercial theatrical lighting design and related fields. Experience with or knowledge of United Scenic Artist, Local 829 is preferred but not required. Candidates must have experience teaching lighting design and production at the college level and a passion for helping emerging designers develop both their artistic voices and technical confidence. We are especially interested in educators who can bring the realities of professional practice into the classroom connecting collaboration, technology, craftsmanship, and storytelling. Expertise in the following areas is expected:\u00a0 Drafting (Hand Drafting, Autocad, and VectorWorks) Lightwright, EOS, and Workflow Best Practices Industry Digital Visualizations Software (i.e. Capture, Light Converse, and Augmented) Programming Production Electrics Projection and video experience is a plus Emerson College is the nation\u2019s only four-year institution dedicated exclusively to undergraduate majors and master\u2019s degrees in communication, arts, and media. It is located in the dynamic, multicultural city of Boston, close to major sports teams, arts institutions, performing arts venues, research centers, and industry partners. Emerson also has campuses in Los Angeles and the Netherlands. At Emerson College, we seek individuals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to our curricular, co-curricular, and extra-curricular offerings. Emerson College believes the best way to achieve excellence is to foster a campus climate where everyone can thrive. As a community of artists, practitioners, scholars, and storytellers, we continually strive to cultivate a collaborative community that draws upon the widest possible pool of talented individuals from varied beliefs, backgrounds, and perspectives. Emerson College\u2019s core values are creativity, innovation, inclusion, curiosity, equity, expression, and collaboration. To Apply Please submit the following: Cover Letter\u00a0 Current Curriculum Vita A digital curated visual portfolio of professional work Statement of teaching philosophy that addresses both the candidate\u2019s approach to mentorship and how the candidate creates learning environments in which everyone has the opportunity to excel Contact information for three references who can speak to the candidate\u2019s professional work and/or teaching\u00a0 Preference will be given to applications received by November 15th, but the position will remain open until filled. Please note that finalists will be invited to campus for in-person teaching demonstrations and interviews during the Spring semester. Please note, in the job application where there is the \"CV/Cover Letter/Additional Documents\" drop box, you must include all of the required materials listed above. You can upload each document separately or as a combined PDF. Your application will not be complete without these documents. If you are having issues uploading, please email facultycareers@emerson.edu. Base salary for this appointment, as set by the CBA, will be $81,723 annually, commensurate with experience and rank of position. Additional salary, supplements, and/or stipends may be available and applicable."}, "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Term-Faculty---Sports-Media-Production_JR009297": {"title": "Term Faculty | Sports Media Production", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJoin our \u00a0 community \u00a0 and experience \u00a0 Emerson College! Emerson College\u2019s Department of Journalism seeks to hire a full-time term faculty member in the area of Sports Media Production. Based in the Journalism Department within the School of Communication, this faculty member will teach on the Boston campus. The appointment begins August 19, 2027, with a mandatory two-day orientation on August 19 & 20, 2027. This faculty member will be expected to teach undergraduate courses in our Sports Media Production concentration in the Journalism major, which also includes Sports Journalism, Live Event Production, and other related courses. The faculty member will also collaborate on a new School-based, College-wide academic center focused on sports leadership, management, communication, and media.\u00a0 College-level teaching experience is preferred. We seek an accomplished sports media professional who will develop new courses and help develop this innovative program for the rapidly growing area of Sports Media Production. Mentoring cross-disciplinary students interested in a sports media production career is also important. Candidates who can teach sports media courses in the department\u2019s online graduate program are encouraged to apply. Applicants should hold at least a bachelor\u2019s degree in journalism or a related field and have professional sports media production experience covering major live sporting events. A terminal master\u2019s degree or higher is preferred but not required. Applicants should demonstrate a record of innovative work in sports media production, reflecting expertise across multiple platforms, formats, social media, and streaming media, as well as working knowledge of fandom, sports production companies, player branding, and emerging technologies. This person will also be expected to strengthen relationships with sports industry partners and develop new ones. Emerson College is the nation\u2019s only four-year institution dedicated exclusively to undergraduate majors and master\u2019s degrees in communication, arts, and media. It is located in the dynamic, multicultural city of Boston, close to major sports teams, arts institutions, performing arts venues, research centers, and industry partners. Emerson also has campuses in Los Angeles and the Netherlands. At Emerson College, we seek individuals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to our curricular, co-curricular, and extra-curricular offerings. Emerson College believes the best way to achieve excellence is to foster a campus climate where everyone can thrive. As a community of artists, practitioners, scholars, and storytellers, we continually strive to cultivate a collaborative community that draws upon the widest possible pool of talented individuals from varied beliefs, backgrounds, and perspectives. Emerson College\u2019s core values are creativity, innovation, inclusion, curiosity, equity, expression, and collaboration. Applicants should submit a CV or resume, a cover letter that speaks to their teaching philosophy and how they create learning environments in which everyone has the opportunity to excel , and the names and contact information for three references. Please note, in the job application where there is the \"CV/Cover Letter/Additional Documents\" drop box, you must include all of the required materials listed above. You can upload each document separately or as a combined PDF. Your application will not be complete without these documents. If you are having issues uploading, please email facultycareers@emerson.edu. Base salary for this appointment, as set by the CBA, will be $81,723 annually, commensurate with experience and rank of position. Additional salary, supplements, and/or stipends may be available and applicable."}, "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Open-Rank--Term-or-Tenure-Track-Tenured----Sports-Communication_JR009302": {"title": "Open Rank (Term or Tenure-Track/Tenured) | Sports Communication", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nJoin our \u00a0 community \u00a0 and experience \u00a0 Emerson College! Emerson College seeks an entrepreneurial sports industry leader and/or scholar to join its nationally recognized Sports Communication program in the Department of Communication Studies. The successful candidate will collaborate with faculty and leaders from across the college to build a premier interdisciplinary academic center in the School of Communication, positioning Emerson as a leading destination for the study and advancement of sports leadership, management, communication, media, culture, and civic life.\u00a0 Rooted in Emerson's mission to educate extraordinary communicators and creators, the successful candidate will teach and mentor in its nationally recognized sports communication program, preparing students to lead in the rapidly-growing global sports ecosystem. The appointment begins August 19, 2027, with a mandatory two-day orientation, August 19 and 20, 2027. Professionals and/or academics with a distinguished record of leadership or scholarship in the sports industry are encouraged to apply, with hands-on experience in leadership and management, communication and public relations, and/or fandom and community engagement preferred. The successful candidate will show evidence of effective collaboration and the ability to engage with leaders internally and externally to build local, national, and global partnerships to support sports industry-related experiential learning and programming.\u00a0 Preferred Requirements: A master\u2019s degree or higher in communication or related fields is preferred, with a bachelor\u2019s degree and at least 10 years of experience required. A distinguished record of leadership and/or scholarship in the sports industry. Prior classroom teaching experience and interdisciplinary curriculum development at the college level in the context of a diverse student community is preferred. In addition to developing an academic center focused on sports leadership, management, communication, and media, the candidate will advise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students. Supporting the theory-practice mission of the Department of Communication Studies, the candidate will have the opportunity to engage in experiential learning with Boston sports teams and programs, and outside Boston with the Washington, D.C. Program, Emerson LA, other teams and leagues, and civic engagement projects.\u00a0 Communication Studies is the first Communication department established in the United States, created at Emerson\u2019s founding in 1880. Its 146-year legacy of nationally recognized leadership in teaching, practicing, and applying the power of communication is the foundation for its undergraduate and graduate programs in Sports Communication; Political Communication: Leadership, Politics and Social Advocacy; and Public Relations. It also offers an undergraduate major in Communication Studies and a graduate program in Digital Communication Leadership.\u00a0\u00a0 Emerson College is the nation\u2019s only four-year institution dedicated exclusively to undergraduate majors and master\u2019s degrees in communication, arts, and media. It is located in the dynamic, multicultural city of Boston, close to major sports teams, arts institutions, performing arts venues, research centers, and industry partners. Emerson also has campuses in Los Angeles and the Netherlands. At Emerson College, we seek individuals who bring innovation, creativity, and impact to our curricular, co-curricular, and extra-curricular offerings. Emerson College believes the best way to achieve excellence is to foster a campus climate where everyone can thrive. As a community of artists, practitioners, scholars, and storytellers, we continually strive to cultivate a collaborative community that draws upon the widest possible pool of talented individuals from varied beliefs, backgrounds, and perspectives. Emerson College\u2019s core values are creativity, innovation, inclusion, curiosity, equity, expression, and collaboration. Applicants should submit a CV or resume, a cover letter that speaks to their teaching philosophy and how they create learning environments in which everyone has the opportunity to excel , and the names and contact information for three references. Please note, in the job application where there is the \"CV/Cover Letter/Additional Documents\" drop box, you must include all of the required materials listed above. You can upload each document separately or as a combined PDF. Your application will not be complete without these documents. If you are having issues uploading, please email facultycareers@emerson.edu. Base salary for this appointment, as set by the CBA, will be $81,723 - $109,042 annually, commensurate with experience and rank of position. Additional salary, supplements, and/or stipends may be available and applicable."}}, "rows": {"https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Term-Faculty---Stage-Management_JR009322": {"school_id": 536, "posting_url": "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Term-Faculty---Stage-Management_JR009322", "job_title_in_post": "Term Faculty | Stage Management", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Term; Stage Management BFA curriculum: Stage", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-14"}, "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Open-Rank--Term-or-Tenure-Track-Tenured-----On-Camera-Acting-and-Scene-Study_JR009321-1": {"school_id": 536, "posting_url": "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Open-Rank--Term-or-Tenure-Track-Tenured-----On-Camera-Acting-and-Scene-Study_JR009321-1", "job_title_in_post": "Open Rank (Term or Tenure-Track/Tenured) |  On-Camera Acting and Scene Study", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Business of Acting", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-14"}, "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Term-Faculty---Lighting-Design_JR009298": {"school_id": 536, "posting_url": "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Term-Faculty---Lighting-Design_JR009298", "job_title_in_post": "Term Faculty | Lighting Design", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Term; Stage Management BFA curriculum: Lighting", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-05"}, "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Term-Faculty---Sports-Media-Production_JR009297": {"school_id": 536, "posting_url": "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Term-Faculty---Sports-Media-Production_JR009297", "job_title_in_post": "Term Faculty | Sports Media Production", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "School of Communication, this faculty member will teach on the Boston campus", "area_key_words": "Term; Sports Media Production concentration", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-05"}, "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Open-Rank--Term-or-Tenure-Track-Tenured----Sports-Communication_JR009302": {"school_id": 536, "posting_url": "https://emerson.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/Emerson_College_ft_faculty/job/Boston-Campus/Open-Rank--Term-or-Tenure-Track-Tenured----Sports-Communication_JR009302", "job_title_in_post": "Open Rank (Term or Tenure-Track/Tenured) | Sports Communication", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor; Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Communication Studies", "area_key_words": "Sports Communication", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": "2026-10-05"}}, "school_id": 536, "status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T18:44:09+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-16T18:44:09+00:00", "last_error": ""}